WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.290 --> 00:00:04.060
SCP-2000 is an unremarkable location.

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:08.730
It is an old, rarely used park ranger station
in Yellowstone National Park.

00:00:08.730 --> 00:00:13.780
It’s in the middle of nowhere and it gets
deliveries of supplies from helicopters and

00:00:13.780 --> 00:00:15.330
unmarked cars as needed.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:22.610
While a few civilians have attempted to break
in, none have been successful and SCP-2000

00:00:22.610 --> 00:00:28.530
remains undisturbed, kept in plain sight without
anything seemingly important about it.

00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:33.180
But why is this one of the most secure locations
in SCP history?

00:00:33.180 --> 00:00:38.160
Why is it of the utmost importance that it
continue to exist, no matter what?

00:00:38.160 --> 00:00:43.810
The answer may rest in a mysterious document
found in the most unlikely of locations.

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:48.850
The Marianas Trench is the deepest point on
Earth, and the SCP Foundation has made many

00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:51.640
trips there to investigate strange phenomena.

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:56.500
But what they recovered on one visit exposed
one of the most closely guarded secrets in

00:00:56.500 --> 00:00:58.399
Foundation history.

00:00:58.399 --> 00:01:03.390
It was a document that had somehow survived
at the bottom of the ocean - sealed in a pipe

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:07.460
and coated in wax to keep it airtight and
waterproof.

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:12.400
It appeared that it had been packaged in such
a way that it could survive anything - and

00:01:12.400 --> 00:01:15.409
that’s exactly what its writer wanted.

00:01:15.409 --> 00:01:20.659
She wasn’t sure when the world had begun
to end, but she could see it coming for a

00:01:20.659 --> 00:01:21.659
while.

00:01:21.659 --> 00:01:24.130
She looked out her window and saw all the
signs.

00:01:24.130 --> 00:01:27.770
The seas were getting colder and less hospitable
to life.

00:01:27.770 --> 00:01:30.310
The air was getting warmer every year.

00:01:30.310 --> 00:01:33.770
Resources were dwindling, and the population
was increasing.

00:01:33.770 --> 00:01:39.190
Tensions were rising, and while no one knew
just when it would come, almost everyone seemed

00:01:39.190 --> 00:01:45.370
sure that the world, or at least humanity,
would reach its conclusion soon.

00:01:45.370 --> 00:01:51.280
It was a sinking ship that first really made
it clear things were going in the wrong direction.

00:01:51.280 --> 00:01:55.900
The Disney Magic was one of the world’s
most popular cruise ships, a favorite vacation

00:01:55.900 --> 00:01:57.460
destination for families.

00:01:57.460 --> 00:02:03.240
It was also one of the most carefully built
ships, as the company prided itself on safety

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:06.689
and had learned well from past cruise ship
tragedies.

00:02:06.689 --> 00:02:11.700
So the world was rightfully shocked when one
day it was announced that the ship had sunk

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.469
while pulling into port.

00:02:13.469 --> 00:02:17.900
No one knew what had happened, and there was
something even more mysterious about this

00:02:17.900 --> 00:02:22.879
tragedy - no one seemed to have any footage
of the sinking.

00:02:22.879 --> 00:02:27.879
Despite round the clock news coverage, all
the pictures were of the ship still afloat.

00:02:27.879 --> 00:02:31.879
That is, until the news companies received
a tape.

00:02:31.879 --> 00:02:36.200
The networks were so eager to play the footage
that none of them reviewed it first and the

00:02:36.200 --> 00:02:38.459
footage went straight to air.

00:02:38.459 --> 00:02:43.419
It showed the ship moving along smoothly,
surrounded by smaller boats, when it suddenly

00:02:43.419 --> 00:02:44.419
stopped.

00:02:44.419 --> 00:02:48.530
It was as if it had been frozen in place,
and the footage showed people on the deck

00:02:48.530 --> 00:02:51.909
of the ship falling over from the abrupt stop.

00:02:51.909 --> 00:02:57.370
Everything went silent, and then an odd foam
emerged from behind the boat.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:59.930
Everyone assumed it was the engine having
issues.

00:02:59.930 --> 00:03:01.709
But it wasn’t the engine.

00:03:01.709 --> 00:03:07.489
It was a massive arm, at least a hundred feet
long and belonging to an eldritch being just

00:03:07.489 --> 00:03:09.150
below the surface.

00:03:09.150 --> 00:03:14.840
It reached up, grabbed the boat, and ripped
it open like a piece of tissue paper.

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:20.029
The thousands of people on board ran for safety,
but there was nowhere they could go.

00:03:20.029 --> 00:03:24.290
Jets zoomed overhead, ready to attack whatever
the thing in the water was.

00:03:24.290 --> 00:03:29.879
A massive, spiny figure started rearing up
out of the water - and then the video went

00:03:29.879 --> 00:03:30.879
black.

00:03:30.879 --> 00:03:35.099
The letter found in the Marianas Trench continued
to explain what happened next -

00:03:35.099 --> 00:03:40.340
The President quickly declared a state of
emergency, and implored everyone to stay calm.

00:03:40.340 --> 00:03:44.609
Television networks were placed under government
control, and were only allowed to broadcast

00:03:44.609 --> 00:03:46.859
government sanctioned information.

00:03:46.859 --> 00:03:51.400
It wasn’t long before the internet became
restricted too, with people prohibited from

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:54.189
sharing information that wasn’t authorized.

00:03:54.189 --> 00:03:58.290
The government just kept telling people to
stay calm and go about their lives.

00:03:58.290 --> 00:04:02.919
The writer of the letter tried to follow this
advice, and went to work and paid her bills

00:04:02.919 --> 00:04:08.129
as if life was still normal...but all around
her she saw terrified faces.

00:04:08.129 --> 00:04:10.919
And they were right to be scared.

00:04:10.919 --> 00:04:16.030
This was only the start of the crisis that
would soon grip the entire world.

00:04:16.030 --> 00:04:20.150
More and more strange things started happening,
but none of them were tied to the mysterious

00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:23.470
monster that had been seen emerging from the
sea.

00:04:23.470 --> 00:04:28.010
Towns were evacuated because of rioting, or
placed under quarantine after an outbreak

00:04:28.010 --> 00:04:30.540
of a mysterious disease.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:33.390
Destruction was blamed on terrorist attacks
or wildfires.

00:04:33.390 --> 00:04:37.100
The writer’s brother called her to tell
her that he had been forced out of his home.

00:04:37.100 --> 00:04:41.670
The reason was supposedly a wildfire, but
he had gotten a chance to look at the fire

00:04:41.670 --> 00:04:45.430
as he was being evacuated, and there was something
odd about it.

00:04:45.430 --> 00:04:53.570
He could swear he saw a figure of a man in
the fire, a man made of fire, and he was moving

00:04:53.570 --> 00:04:54.820
deliberately.

00:04:54.820 --> 00:04:58.450
But she couldn’t ask any questions about
what he had seen because the call got dropped

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:01.031
- and she never got to speak to her brother
again.

00:05:01.031 --> 00:05:06.120
It was becoming harder and harder to get any
information about what was happening.

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:10.340
With most news sources shut down or under
strict government control, there were only

00:05:10.340 --> 00:05:13.010
vague rumors for her to latch onto.

00:05:13.010 --> 00:05:17.630
People talked about zombies ravaging the north,
about people who seemed normal one moment

00:05:17.630 --> 00:05:20.300
losing their minds and going on killing sprees.

00:05:20.300 --> 00:05:25.260
There were whispers of a doomsday cult rising
up that was trying to stem the apocalypse

00:05:25.260 --> 00:05:27.450
through human sacrifices.

00:05:27.450 --> 00:05:31.940
There was even talk about the ground itself
coming to life and eating people.

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:36.380
It all sounded like one thing - the end of
the world.

00:05:36.380 --> 00:05:41.200
The letter’s writer tried to stay sane,
keeping her information intake to a minimum

00:05:41.200 --> 00:05:45.050
and attempting to go about her life in as
normal a way as she could.

00:05:45.050 --> 00:05:50.110
But it wouldn’t be long before the horrors
outside came to find her, and they became

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:51.521
impossible to ignore.

00:05:51.521 --> 00:05:56.130
It was early in the morning when she heard
screaming and gunshots outside.

00:05:56.130 --> 00:06:01.020
She could smell something burning, and found
blood smeared on her window, but she was too

00:06:01.020 --> 00:06:03.450
scared to find out what was happening.

00:06:03.450 --> 00:06:06.400
She hid and waited for the noise to die down.

00:06:06.400 --> 00:06:11.150
Soon the power and heating went out, and her
water supply cut off not long after.

00:06:11.150 --> 00:06:15.570
She knew she would have to go outside if she
wanted to survive, and she wasn’t prepared

00:06:15.570 --> 00:06:19.510
for what she would find - or rather, what
she wouldn’t.

00:06:19.510 --> 00:06:24.500
Her house was in a flat suburban area, without
any major geographical landmarks.

00:06:24.500 --> 00:06:29.300
So she wasn’t expecting to step outside
and find a massive cliff with the other side

00:06:29.300 --> 00:06:31.240
nowhere to be seen.

00:06:31.240 --> 00:06:35.310
Not only did it look like the rest of the
world had fallen away, but she couldn’t

00:06:35.310 --> 00:06:37.060
see the bottom of the cliff.

00:06:37.060 --> 00:06:39.860
It was like that half of the world no longer
existed.

00:06:39.860 --> 00:06:46.040
What was left of her neighborhood had been
torn apart, with blood and destruction everywhere.

00:06:46.040 --> 00:06:49.040
And she seemed to be the only person left.

00:06:49.040 --> 00:06:51.150
Had she been saved because she hid?

00:06:51.150 --> 00:06:54.400
Or had the others taken the opportunity to
evacuate?

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:58.470
She didn’t know, but all the houses around
her had been abandoned.

00:06:58.470 --> 00:07:03.190
She was determined to survive, and so she
took what supplies she needed from the empty

00:07:03.190 --> 00:07:05.740
homes and retreated back to her own.

00:07:05.740 --> 00:07:10.160
It soon became clear though that much more
had changed than just the geography of the

00:07:10.160 --> 00:07:11.160
world.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:13.880
Time itself seemed to be slowing down.

00:07:13.880 --> 00:07:18.910
The sun stood still in the sky, not moving
from one spot for days.

00:07:18.910 --> 00:07:23.830
Sometimes a heavy fog would quickly roll in,
and render her essentially blind.

00:07:23.830 --> 00:07:28.540
But worst of all, she soon found that she
was no longer alone.

00:07:28.540 --> 00:07:32.470
Whatever had come into her neighborhood now,
it wasn’t human.

00:07:32.470 --> 00:07:36.710
The first to come were strange, roughly man
sized metal creatures.

00:07:36.710 --> 00:07:41.240
Then came the smaller creatures, like the
one that looked like a pillbug, but one the

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:43.090
size of a cat.

00:07:43.090 --> 00:07:47.980
This one seemed harmless at first, but then
it looked at her and screamed “STOP” in

00:07:47.980 --> 00:07:49.760
a human voice.

00:07:49.760 --> 00:07:55.960
But this was nothing compared to what came
next - giant, blimp-like maggots with hundreds

00:07:55.960 --> 00:07:57.210
of eyes.

00:07:57.210 --> 00:08:02.170
They were ferocious predators, landing and
eating anything in sight.

00:08:02.170 --> 00:08:06.780
She was sure with all of these horrors, that
she must be the only human left, but one day

00:08:06.780 --> 00:08:11.000
after one of the disgusting blimps passed
by she found someone else.

00:08:11.000 --> 00:08:15.360
He looked like he belonged to a SWAT team,
and was clearly hurt.

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:19.820
Seeing another human was enough to spur her
into action, and she pulled him to safety

00:08:19.820 --> 00:08:20.940
in her home.

00:08:20.940 --> 00:08:23.930
He told her that he had been hunting one of
the blimp-maggots.

00:08:23.930 --> 00:08:27.830
She told him that he was the first person
she had seen since the cliff showed up in

00:08:27.830 --> 00:08:31.460
her neighborhood and the rest of the world
had disappeared.

00:08:31.460 --> 00:08:33.620
His response to this was odd though.

00:08:33.620 --> 00:08:36.050
He told her that the world hadn’t disappeared.

00:08:36.050 --> 00:08:40.329
It had simply “relocated” but couldn’t
tell her any more than that.

00:08:40.329 --> 00:08:44.410
She pressed him for more information, and
he said that his orders really meant nothing

00:08:44.410 --> 00:08:45.410
anymore.

00:08:45.410 --> 00:08:49.740
He revealed that he worked for a foundation
that tracked down strange and dangerous creatures

00:08:49.740 --> 00:08:53.730
and captured them for research and to keep
the world safe.

00:08:53.730 --> 00:08:56.200
But something had gone wrong.

00:08:56.200 --> 00:09:00.259
All the entities they had been keeping contained
had broken free at the same time.

00:09:00.259 --> 00:09:05.809
It was too late to reverse the damage, and
the world had been declared a “GH-0 Dead

00:09:05.809 --> 00:09:07.610
Greenhouse” scenario.

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:11.930
The foundation had failed, but there was a
plan.

00:09:11.930 --> 00:09:17.019
There were still people alive, but carefully
contained around the world in safe zones.

00:09:17.019 --> 00:09:22.730
The Foundation had a way to reboot the world,
including recreating people with all the memories

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:23.730
intact.

00:09:23.730 --> 00:09:28.129
The Foundation would clear out the dangerous
entities, repair the damage, and use their

00:09:28.129 --> 00:09:31.290
technology to put everything back as it was.

00:09:31.290 --> 00:09:36.050
This world would be gone, but it would be
replaced with another one that resembled itself

00:09:36.050 --> 00:09:39.249
exactly - with no memories of the horrors
that had occurred.

00:09:39.249 --> 00:09:40.249
She recoiled in horror.

00:09:40.249 --> 00:09:41.600
This couldn’t be done, right?

00:09:41.600 --> 00:09:44.399
It was impossible to sweep all of this away.

00:09:44.399 --> 00:09:46.350
He just smiled and said “Why not?

00:09:46.350 --> 00:09:48.089
It’s been done before?”

00:09:48.089 --> 00:09:50.540
She didn’t know when the end would come.

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:53.209
She didn’t even know if she would realize
it was happening.

00:09:53.209 --> 00:09:55.749
But she didn’t want to be forgotten.

00:09:55.749 --> 00:09:58.980
So she wrote her thoughts down and sealed
them in a tube.

00:09:58.980 --> 00:10:01.430
She sealed the tube in wax and waited.

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:03.860
Maybe her house wouldn’t be fully destroyed.

00:10:03.860 --> 00:10:07.570
Maybe it would wind up underwater as the man
had briefly mentioned.

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:12.160
Maybe her message would endure and be found
one day, as the last relic of a world that

00:10:12.160 --> 00:10:13.730
had been wiped away.

00:10:13.730 --> 00:10:18.369
She wouldn’t be around to see it, but maybe
her world would be remembered.

00:10:18.369 --> 00:10:23.600
The true purpose of SCP-2000 is the Foundation’s
most closely guarded secret.

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:29.129
A massive underground facility designed to
prevent humanity’s extinction, able to produce

00:10:29.129 --> 00:10:31.540
over a hundred thousand humans per day.

00:10:31.540 --> 00:10:37.329
It contains memory banks that hold the entire
history of the human species and all associated

00:10:37.329 --> 00:10:38.449
information.

00:10:38.449 --> 00:10:43.259
But all documentation regarding its initial
construction and history has been lost, though

00:10:43.259 --> 00:10:49.170
no one is sure whether this information was
lost in one of the resets - or by design.

00:10:49.170 --> 00:10:53.480
The Foundation has made sure that SCP-2000
will not be breached.

00:10:53.480 --> 00:10:57.930
The facility is guarded by cognitohazards
that will stop anyone without the appropriate

00:10:57.930 --> 00:10:59.230
inoculation.

00:10:59.230 --> 00:11:04.160
Any unauthorized access attempts are considered
grounds for instant termination regardless

00:11:04.160 --> 00:11:07.390
of how high-ranking someone might be in the
Foundation.

00:11:07.390 --> 00:11:13.300
SCP-2000 is to the Foundation what the Svalbard
Global Seed Vault is to agriculture - the

00:11:13.300 --> 00:11:16.240
fail-safe in case everything goes wrong.

00:11:16.240 --> 00:11:21.579
That’s why it has the object class of Thaumiel,
a rare classification that is secret to all

00:11:21.579 --> 00:11:24.360
but the highest levels of the Foundation.

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:29.420
But to almost everyone, including every SCP
Foundation member who has never encountered

00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:36.620
it, SCP-2000 is just an old, rarely used park
ranger station in Yellowstone National Park,

00:11:36.620 --> 00:11:41.350
with absolutely nothing unique about it, and
no reason to look closer.

00:11:41.350 --> 00:11:44.839
And the Foundation will ensure it stays that
way.

00:11:44.839 --> 00:11:49.240
That’s why when, a letter was found at the
bottom of the Marianas trench that describes

00:11:49.240 --> 00:11:54.019
one of these world resetting scenarios, a
letter that pleads to not let the world that

00:11:54.019 --> 00:12:00.550
existed before be forgotten, or hidden away,
the Foundation made sure with absolute certainty,

00:12:00.550 --> 00:12:02.959
that it would never see the light of day.

00:12:02.959 --> 00:12:10.550
Now, for more on SCP facilities, check out
SCP-2000 Deus Ex Machina or the entire saga

00:12:10.550 --> 00:12:13.739
of SCP-1730 and what happened at the mysterious
Site-13.

